Quick guidance for travel to Italy (Schengen rules) and general visa practice:
- Schengen (including Italy) requires your passport be valid for at least 3 months beyond your planned date of departure from the Schengen area, and it must have been issued within the last 10 years. 
- Some airlines and some countries/embassies require 6 months’ validity as a stricter rule. Many people renew if their passport has under 6 months remaining to avoid any risk with airlines or visa processing.
- If you’re applying for a visa, many consulates ask for at least 6 months’ validity at the time of application.

What I recommend:
