- Some countries and some airlines recommend — or enforce — a 6-month minimum validity, so many travelers renew if they have fewer than 6 months remaining to avoid any risk.
- If your passport will have less than 3 months validity beyond your planned exit date from Schengen, you should definitely renew before travel. If it’s between 3 and 6 months remaining, you’re likely okay for Italy/Schengen but renewing is the safer option (airlines can be strict).
- If you need to renew, you can usually do standard or expedited renewal through your country’s passport agency; processing times vary, so check expedited options if your travel is soon.

Tell me the passport expiration date (and confirm nationality) and I’ll tell you whether it’s acceptable for travel to Italy and whether I recommend renewing — and I can draft any renewal or consulate email if you want.

