Key guidance right away (short version):
- Schengen/Italy rule: passports should generally be valid for at least 3 months beyond your planned date of departure from the Schengen area and be issued within the last 10 years.
- Many airlines and some countries (and travel advisors) recommend or enforce a 6‑month minimum validity to avoid denied boarding. So even though Schengen’s formal rule is 3 months, a 6‑month buffer is the safer rule of thumb.
- Practical recommendation: If your passport will expire less than 6 months after your planned return date, renew it before you travel to avoid problems with airlines or border agents.

