What to do now
- If your passport expires less than six months after your trip ends: renew before you travel.
- If it expires between 3 and 6 months after your trip end: you may be allowed entry in some cases (Schengen allows 3 months), but you risk being denied boarding by the airline — renewing is recommended.
- If it expires less than 3 months after your trip end: you should definitely renew.

Renewal options and timing
- Renewal processing times vary by country and current demand. Expedited services are usually available for an extra fee. Check your government’s passport agency website for current processing times and expedite options.
- If time is tight, look into booking an expedited appointment at a passport agency (or a private expediting service) and confirm what documentation and fees are required.

