I can help — first a couple quick safety and clarification items:

- Don’t post your full SSN here (you already redacted most — good). I don’t need your SSN to answer this question.
- Tell me your passport expiry date and your planned travel dates (departure and return) and whether you mean a short-stay Schengen/tourist visa or a different visa type. With those I can check the rules for Italy/Schengen and tell you if your passport validity is sufficient.

General guidance while you gather details:
- Schengen (Italy) short-stay visa rule: your passport must be valid for at least 3 months beyond your intended date of departure from the Schengen area, and it must have been issued within the last 10 years. So if you plan to leave Schengen on, say, Sept 1, your passport should be valid through at least Dec 1.
- Many airlines and some countries recommend (or require) 6 months’ passport validity beyond your travel dates. Even when Schengen’s official minimum is 3 months, renewing if you have under 6 months remaining is often wise to avoid boarding/entry problems.
- Also ensure you have at least two blank passport pages for visa stamps.

If you give me:
- passport expiry date and
- your planned arrival and departure dates (or the visa length if that’s fixed),
I’ll tell you whether the expiry is too close and recommend next steps (renewal options, expedite timelines, or whether you should be OK).

