- Many airlines and some countries — and practical advice from travel experts — recommend a 6‑month minimum passport validity to avoid problems boarding or entering, so renewing if your passport has less than 6 months remaining is prudent.
- If you’re applying for a visa that would be valid for six months, the issuing authority may require that your passport be valid at least through the visa’s period (or for some additional time beyond it). Requirements can vary by consulate.

