Thanks — a few quick points and then I can help more precisely.

1) About the SSN
- Please avoid posting your full SSN in chats or emails. If you must share for a form, give only the last 4 digits when possible. I noticed the numbers you posted look inconsistent (***-**-7890 vs last four 6789) — double-check that before submitting any forms.

2) Passport / visa validity — general guidance
- Schengen (Italy) standard rule: your passport should be valid for at least 3 months beyond your planned date of departure from the Schengen area and must have been issued within the last 10 years. 
- However, many consulates/airlines recommend — or require for some visas — 6 months of validity beyond your planned stay. Some visa categories explicitly require 6 months.
- If your passport expiry is less than 6 months after your planned entry date, you may run into airline check-in or visa issues even if Schengen lists 3 months. It’s safer to renew if you’re within 6 months of expiry.

3) What I need to give specific advice
- Tell me: your passport expiry date (month/year) and your planned travel dates (arrival and departure). Also tell me whether you’re applying for a Schengen short-stay (tourist) visa or traveling visa-free as a U.S. passport holder — that changes the exact requirement.

4) If you need to renew quickly
- Options include expedited renewal through your national passport agency (in the U.S. you can pay for expedited service or get an urgent appointment at a regional agency if travel is within 2–3 weeks). I can draft a checklist or an email to the passport agency or consulate for you.

Which would you like to do next? Provide your passport expiry and travel dates and I’ll tell you whether it’s likely to be a problem and give next steps (or draft any email you need).

